Fork-local patch, not part of radxa-pkg's debian/patches series.

The USB rx path prints "rx eapol" with a bare printk() for every received
EAPOL frame. It has no log level of its own and ignores aicwf_dbg_level
(which fix-Lower-the-debugging-log-level sets to LOGERROR), so it lands on
the console at the default level and floods it on every WPA handshake and
rekey. Route it through AICWFDBG(LOGDEBUG, ...) like the neighbouring
traces.

The PCIE tree has a similar txrx_err() print; this system builds only
the USB driver, so it is left alone.

--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
@@ -2529,7 +2529,7 @@
 
 
             if((ether_type[0] == 0x8e && ether_type[1] == 0x88) || (ether_type[0] == 0x88 && ether_type[1] == 0x8e))
-                printk("rx eapol\n");
+                AICWFDBG(LOGDEBUG, "rx eapol\n");
 			
 			if (is_amsdu) {
 //Check NETGEAR R7000 router's AMSDU packet format for compliance. start
